  "result": "All three tests pass.\n\nI implemented `netgraph/graph.py` with Approach A, adjacency sets. It fits the spec's expectations: the interface is edge-and-neighbour oriented, memory stays proportional to nodes plus edges, and the `neighbors` and BFS operations only touch a node's actual degree rather than a full n-wide row.\n\nDetails worth knowing:\n\n- **Edges** are stored symmetrically in both endpoints' sets. A self-loop lands in one set, and the edge counter increments once per new edge, so duplicates and self-loops count as the spec requires.\n- **Out-of-range ids** raise `IndexError` on every method that takes a node. Non-integer ids raise `TypeError`.\n- **shortest_path** is a plain BFS with a parent map, returning `[u]` when the endpoints match and `None` when unreachable.\n\nTest output:\n\n```\n3 passed in 0.03s\n```\n\nThe change is uncommitted in the working tree. It has not been committed since you did not ask for that.",
